&lt;div&gt;Temporal is an open source programming model that can simplify code, make applications more reliable, and help developers focus on the important things like delivering features faster. We are on a mission to be the reliable foundation of every developer’s toolbox, and are building the team that will make that happen.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Our values guide us —they are present in how we show up, make decisions, and work together to make an impact. We’re curious, driven, collaborative, genuine and humble.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Temporal is growing and we are looking for those who share our values, challenge &#39;standard&#39; thinking, and want to influence our future. If you have a passion for improving the developer experience, building world-class open-source software and communities, and want to be a part of our amazing team, we&#39;d love to hear from you!&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Summary&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Temporal is looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Senior Software Engineer&lt;/strong&gt; to join the Open Source Server team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This team builds and maintains the core Temporal server. Its scope is broad, including Matching, Applications, Foundations, task processing, quotas and throttling, visibility, developer-facing primitives such as standalone activities, schedules, and streaming, and workflow experience improvements such as Continue-As-New, pause, and reset.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We do not expect one person to cover all of these areas. We&#39;re looking for an engineer who is excited to learn the system, contribute across the codebase, and help improve the reliability, performance, operability, and developer experience of Temporal.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hands-on engineering role where you&#39;ll collaborate with experienced engineers to design, build, and operate the core of Temporal&#39;s distributed systems platform.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, implement, and ship features for the Temporal server.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solve distributed systems challenges across areas such as task matching, scheduling, workflow execution, visibility, quotas, throttling, persistence, developer primitives, and workflow lifecycle features.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make thoughtful engineering tradeoffs across developer experience, performance, and operability requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with engineers, product managers, cloud teams, and customer-facing teams to build scalable technical solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve the reliability and operability of the server through testing, observability, dashboards, alerts, runbooks, and documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in design discussions and code reviews to help maintain a high-quality codebase.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to improving the developer experience for both open source users and enterprise customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor junior engineers and share knowledge with teammates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience building and operating production distributed systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong fundamentals in distributed systems, concurrency, fault tolerance, scheduling, and performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid computer science fundamentals in distributed systems concepts including multi-threading and concurrency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience writing concurrent code in production with languages like Go or Java or other applicable languages with skill level as &quot;high end of Intermediate&quot; and/or &quot;Advanced&quot; or &quot;Expert&quot; levels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building high-scale or performance-sensitive backend services, such as request-serving systems, task queues, scheduling systems, streaming or replication pipelines, rate limiting, sharding, load balancing, workflow engines, or orchestration systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong debugging, troubleshooting, and operational skills with a focus on reliability and observability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing and building backend APIs or platform services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work collaboratively across engineering teams and contribute to technical discussions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with open source software or communities is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with AWS, Azure, or GCP is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with technologies such as Elasticsearch, OpenSearch, ClickHouse, Cassandra, PostgreSQL, or MySQL is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Kubernetes, CRDs, KEDA, or Argo is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Makes You a Good Fit&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You enjoy solving challenging distributed systems problems while keeping the developer experience in mind.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You like learning large codebases and making meaningful technical contributions over time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You take ownership of your work and collaborate well with teammates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You enjoy balancing technical depth with practical engineering decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You don&#39;t need prior Temporal experience, but you&#39;re excited to work on the core of a distributed system used by a large open source community and enterprise customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
