&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Temporal is an open source programming model that can simplify code, make applications more reliable, and help developers focus on the important things like delivering features faster. We are on a mission to be the reliable foundation of every developer’s toolbox, and are building the team that will make that happen.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Our values guide us —they are present in how we show up, make decisions, and work together to make an impact. We’re curious, driven, collaborative, genuine and humble.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Temporal is growing and we are looking for those who share our values, challenge &#39;standard&#39; thinking, and want to influence our future. If you have a passion for improving the developer experience, building world-class open-source software and communities, and want to be a part of our amazing team, we&#39;d love to hear from you!&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;Overview&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Temporal Cloud is Temporal’s managed SaaS product, used by customers to run workloads with varying requirements for throughput, latency, resilience, isolation, data residency, and cost. Namespaces are the primary unit of isolation within Temporal Cloud.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role you’ll own the Cloud Namespace product surface end-to-end: ensuring customers can provision, configure, operate, and evolve Namespaces safely and effectively over time. You’ll partner with engineering teams to deliver customer-facing capabilities and shape internal operational systems for namespace placement, provisioning, capacity management, and more.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the &lt;strong&gt;full&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;strong&gt;Cloud Namespace lifecycle&lt;/strong&gt; for an operator using Temporal Cloud: understanding workload needs, provisioning and management flows, defining the right configuration defaults and policies, updates-in-place, and safe deletion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and evolve &lt;strong&gt;differentiated Namespace offerings&lt;/strong&gt; (e.g., higher/lower SLA, latency, durability, residency, and cost options) that are easy for customers to understand and trust.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own &lt;strong&gt;throughput and capacity management&lt;/strong&gt; for Namespaces (e.g., autoscaling, TRUs, reserved vs. elastic capacity, scheduling, visibility, limits, and quotas).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive &lt;strong&gt;operational policy and features&lt;/strong&gt; (Namespace placement in deployment rings, replication, scaling) to deliver highly performant, reliable, and cost-effective service at massive multi-tenant scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and own &lt;strong&gt;Namespace SLOs and SLAs&lt;/strong&gt;, including instrumentation and customer-facing communication of performance and reliability expectations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the &lt;strong&gt;Namespace APIs &amp;amp; configuration&lt;/strong&gt; used by customer automation, the Temporal Cloud UI, and other products and services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What You’ll Bring&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Product leadership experience shipping and operating &lt;strong&gt;platform/infrastructure products&lt;/strong&gt;, especially where reliability, performance, and cost tradeoffs matter.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong systems thinking: ability to translate workload needs into &lt;strong&gt;tiering, pricing, policy, quotas/limits, and defaults&lt;/strong&gt; that scale across many customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort partnering closely with engineering on technical topics like &lt;strong&gt;autoscaling, capacity planning, rolling deployment and placement logic&lt;/strong&gt;, and resilience patterns—even if you’re not writing production code.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience defining and managing &lt;strong&gt;SLOs/SLAs&lt;/strong&gt; and using metrics to drive product decisions and prioritization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to build alignment across stakeholders (Engineering, Cloud Ops/SRE, Support, Sales, Solutions, Security) and make clear, durable decisions in ambiguous environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear written and verbal communication, including the ability to produce crisp PRDs, decision docs, and customer-facing explanations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Nice to Haves&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with multi-tenant systems, workload isolation, and “noisy neighbor” mitigation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with API product design for long-lived resource lifecycle operations and safe evolution over time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background working on placement, routing, data residency, or geo-distributed reliability problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building pricing/packaging inputs for tiered services in partnership with Finance/GTM.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
