&lt;p&gt;We are a high-growth, private, consumption-based software company seeking a Vice President, Global Controller to build and lead our accounting, tax, treasury, and procurement functions. This is a rare opportunity for a hands-on financial leader to own the full accounting and operating infrastructure of a scaling business, partner closely with the CFO and executive team, and help architect the systems, controls, and international footprint needed to support the company&#39;s next phase of growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own all aspects of global accounting operations, including the monthly and quarterly close, consolidations, technical accounting (including usage-based/consumption revenue recognition under ASC 606), and financial reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead corporate tax strategy and compliance, including domestic and international tax planning, transfer pricing, and indirect tax (sales/use, VAT/GST) as the company expands globally.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and manage treasury operations: cash management, banking relationships, FX exposure, and capital deployment across multiple currencies and entities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own global procurement and vendor management: source-to-pay processes, vendor contract negotiation, spend management, and purchasing policies/controls as the company scales.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and scale accounting infrastructure, systems, and processes (ERP, billing, and close automation) to support rapid consumption-based revenue growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish and maintain a strong internal control environment (SOX-ready), including policies, procedures, and audit readiness in anticipation of a future public offering or transaction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead all aspects of the annual financial statement audit and manage relationships with external auditors, tax advisors, and banking partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Guide international expansion from a finance and accounting perspective: entity structuring, local statutory and tax compliance, and building out finance operations in new markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with the CFO and cross-functional leaders (Legal, Sales, Revenue Operations) on deal structuring, contract review, and revenue recognition for new consumption-based pricing models.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build, mentor, and scale a high-performing global accounting and tax team as the organization grows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver accurate, timely financial reporting to executive leadership, the board of directors, and investors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;12+ years of progressive accounting/finance experience, including significant leadership experience in a high-growth SaaS or consumption/usage-based software company for both private and public companies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CPA required; Big 4 public accounting background strongly preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep expertise in US GAAP, including ASC 606 revenue recognition for consumption/usage-based models.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience building or scaling tax and treasury functions, including international tax and multi-entity/multi-currency operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of scaling accounting infrastructure and teams through periods of rapid growth, ideally including international expansion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience preparing an organization for an IPO is strongly preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience owning or partnering closely with procurement/vendor management, including contract negotiation and spend controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong systems acumen (e.g., NetSuite, Workday, or similar ERP; billing platforms for usage-based revenue).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and executive presence; able to partner directly with the CFO, CEO, board, and investors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Accounting or Finance; MBA a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
